! v0.74.x Stage 2.2a -- geometry optimization with PCM via FD gradient.
!
! HF/STO-3G water in IEFPCM water (eps = 78.36).  Starting from the
! v0.73 reference geometry (slightly stretched O-H).  The optimizer
! is the internal-coords RFO with FD-PCM gradients at every step.
!
! Reference (this commit):
!   Steps to converge:  6  (max_geom_iter = 30 budget)
!   Final energy:      -74.971153664988 Ha
!   Final r(O-H):       0.9875 Angstrom
!   Final angle H-O-H:  100.0 degrees
!
! Tight-converge tolerance trips on max|g|, RMS|g|, max|dx|, RMS|dx|.
! Loosened grad_tol from the default 3e-4 to 1e-3 because the FD floor
! (~ 1e-7) plus the PCM switching noise floor make 3e-4 a strict
! target -- tightening would require either a smaller h (worsening
! round-off) or analytical gradients (Stage 2.2b).
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     opt
%solvent water
%geom_maxiter 30
%grad_tol 1.0e-3
%geom angstrom
O  0.000000   0.000000   0.119262
H  0.000000   0.755453  -0.477047
H  0.000000  -0.755453  -0.477047
*end
